   "note": "Designed a block with a cyclic entanglement topology (ring CNOTs) to respect the permutation symmetry of the graph connectivity problem. The structure uses RZ rotations for phase encoding, followed by a ring of CNOTs to entangle neighbors, then RY rotations for amplitude modulation, and finally another ring of CNOTs to disentangle/propagate correlations. This creates a translationally invariant ansatz where the interaction pattern is uniform across all nodes, allowing the model to learn global connectivity features (like full connectivity) rather than position-dependent artifacts. The cyclic shift generator in the hypothesis reflects this symmetry.",
